{"id": "EUVD-2026-103754", "enisaUuid": "63681b40-9035-39cb-9bdf-c615bfd43dc8", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/nouveau: Fix gem reference leak in validate_init()\n\nOn the ttm_bo_reserve() failure and \"vma not found\" error paths, the\nloop breaks without adding the looked-up object to any validate list,\nso the reference taken by drm_gem_object_lookup() is never released;\nvalidate_fini() only walks the spliced lists.  Drop the reference\nbefore breaking out on both paths.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:17:30", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:20:54", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/af2f48c12365866abb327d75c21a13bbde84719c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3c80e069470cf73c357c9edb5ec5fba20e6f6a98", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/957619120c26d6727efd18504e6b488673d3900a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/74485cdc343060fce08f8f3990da524d783e43a7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8281930fc194ad448aaa5de8dd47fb6fb1cba327", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/030e93fc91d55d9487b3b85fc0712bb795d77834", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9e13c398a23445baf38f0a59033dd9872a2bfe20", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5ea72f7b7139b123713a7983448f910bc4514d9e"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98514", "GHSA-g33v-35j5-pxgw"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0126a793-bbe5-3607-827f-23859b3d3af1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "19ca10d82e33bcfe92412c461fc3534ec1e14747 <8281930fc194ad448aaa5de8dd47fb6fb1cba327"}, {"id": "045c38ae-2947-36ce-8991-e24fb4917e17", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.17.12 <4.18"}, {"id": "05248daa-73dd-3bfa-a869-ca3e18dfb838", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "23d047bd-1d63-3e93-ae37-23ed26abbdd7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "19ca1